\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. For those we love within the veil,
\par Who once were comrades of our way,
\par We thank Thee, Lord; for they have won
\par To cloudless day;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. And life for them is life indeed,
\par The splendid goal of earth's 
\par strait race;
\par And where no shadows intervene,
\par They see Thy face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Not as we knew them any more,
\par Toilworn, and sad with burdened care-
\par Erect, clear- eyed, upon their brows
\par Thy name thy bear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Free from the fret of mortal years,
\par And knowing now Thy perfect will,
\par With quickened sense and heightened joy
\par They serve Thee still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O fuller, sweeter is that life,
\par Amd larger, ampler is the air:
\par Eye cannot see nor heart conceive
\par The glory there;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Nor know to what high purpose Thou
\par Dost yet employ their ripened powers,
\par Now how  at Thy behest they touch 
\par This life of ours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. There are no tears within their eyes;
\par With love they keep perpetual tryst;
\par And praise and work and rest are one,
\par With Thee, O Christ.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

